FILED s525 (Fable, 2026-10-24) by the round-4 board attribution (review/attrib-r4/: one-file runs on -38 -39 -40 -41 -42 -43; PASS 2/0 on -38 and -39, 1/1 from -40 = s522b, the stash batch: "a non-CODE stash element READS as its typeglob" + the stash view widened past #1510's subs-only list).  Warm and COLD cache alike (review/attrib-r4/COLD.*: not the #2702 first-run shape).

PROBE (scratchpad p525p/codeslot.pl), perl 5.40.3 vs PCL main 95c4fe37 vs wt-main39:
  package Foo; sub f { my ($ok, $reason) = (1, ""); $ok }
  package main; sub ok { 1 } no strict "refs";
  my @keys = sort keys %Foo::; my @code = grep { *{"Foo::$_"}{CODE} } @keys; print "keys=@keys\ncode=@code\n";
  perl:      keys=f / code=f
  PCL main:  keys=f ok reason / code=f      <- the lexicals leak into the stash view
  PCL -39:   keys=f / code=f
The minimal probe shows the KEY leak, not the CODE slot; the dist file shows both: `tools/run-dist-t.pl --rows ~/.cpan/build/HTTP-Tiny-0.090-0 t/001_api.t` -> `# Found: ok`, i.e. `*{"HTTP::Tiny::ok"}{CODE}` answers true for the leaked name (HTTP/Tiny.pm:556 `my($ok, $reason) = (1, "")` inside can_ssl; main has Test::More's ok).  Find why the CODE slot reads true there (the :invert reader? an inherited symbol? the typeglob-value rule of s522b?) -- the fix is in the stash view: a stash lists GLOBS (subs, package vars, filehandles), never a lexical's symbol.  Layer: cl/pcl-runtime.lisp (the stash view) or the emission that interns lexical names into the CL package.

Board row: HTTP-Tiny-0.090-0 001_api.t #2 blessed with this cause (s525); its LOST twin (2 -> 1 passing) is the same row.  Acceptance: the probe prints keys=f; the one-file run 2/0; the row leaves baselines/cpan-board14-fails.tsv by edit.
